  "body": "Found while finishing PR #1618 (#1614). PR #1632 (#1616) is merged.\n\n**What happens.** In `grblhal.cps` and `carvera.cps`, a stream that states no clearance plane and no retract plane is refused by name. But `onRapid` calls `xyFirst` and then still writes the combined `G0 X.. Y.. Z..`. The app blocks the post on the warning (`posting.rs:588`). The `post` CLI (`crates/post/src/bin/post.rs:163`) writes the file anyway and gives the warning on stderr. Thus the refused move is in the program text.\n\nThe Fanuc family (#1636) and Tormach (#1618) write no motion after this refusal. TinyG returns `false` from `startXY`.\n\n**Expected.** After the refusal, grblHAL and Carvera write no motion for the rest of the section, as the other posts do. The refusal pin asserts that the program has no X/Y motion.\n\n**Done means:** `first_traverse_clearance::a_first_traverse_with_no_stated_plane_is_refused_by_name` asserts that there is no X/Y motion line for grblHAL, Carvera and TinyG. It is red on today's code for grblHAL and Carvera.\n",
